L	Artybug	Karo'et-pattern Siege Crawler. UNSC designation: Beetle. A Covenant war beast, a purple-shelled walker spiked with red armour plates, with a plasma cannon at its front that fires a spray of bolts like a shotgun. It takes a great deal of punishment, and it will rush anything that gets close.
L	Draeth	A warrior race of the Covenant, kin to the Sangheili in build and bearing, in an older style of armour. UNSC troops who met them called them Reavers. They fight like Elites with the Covenant's guns: plasma rifles and needlers, and fuel rod cannons in the hands of Majors. Only their high ranks wear energy shields; Minors and Majors fight unshielded. Their color tells their rank: blue Minors, red Majors, white Commanders, gold Zealots.
L	DraethCommander	A Draeth commander in white. Commanders carry the Covenant's heavier arms: a beam rifle for the long shot, a Plasma Caster that lobs clusters of plasma over cover, or a fuel rod cannon. Many go into battle under active camouflage, trading their shield for the cloak; watch for the shimmer.
L	DraethZealot	A Draeth zealot in gold, above the commanders: the most devout of their warriors, tougher than any other Draeth and behind the strongest shield of their kind, armed with the commanders' heavy weapons.
L	Elite	Sangheili. The Covenant's warrior caste and its field officers: tall, fast, and protected by a recharging energy shield. They command the lesser races, roll out of grenade blasts, and fall back to let their shields return before pressing again. Their armor color tells their rank.
L	EliteCommander	A gold-armored Commander, veteran of many campaigns. Commanders lead from the front and favor the energy sword.
L	EliteHeavy	A green-armored Elite trusted with heavier weapons, the fuel rod among them. Heavies sit between Majors and Commanders in rank.
L	EliteHonorGuard	The High Council's ceremonial guard, chosen from the Sangheili's finest and armored in crimson and gold. They guard the Prophets themselves, and the sword is their weapon of choice.
L	EliteMajor	A red-armored Major. Stronger shields than a Minor, better aim, and a commander's habit of directing the Grunts around it.
L	EliteMinor	The blue-armored Minor Domo, the lowest Elite rank and still the most dangerous soldier in most Covenant squads.
L	EliteRanger	Sangheili trained to fight in vacuum and on hostile ground, sealed in an EVA suit and carried by a jump pack. Rangers take the high ground in a fight and drift down onto you from above.
L	EliteSpecial	Sangheili special operations, in black armor with active camouflage. They strike from concealment and are seldom seen until they choose to be.
L	EliteSpecops	Spec Ops Elites: picked warriors with stronger shields and better weapons, assigned to the operations that matter. They work alongside the Spec Ops Grunts.
L	Geist	A small, sleek Covenant attack drone that hunts in packs. Each one carries a plasma rifle under its hull and dives in to strafe its target before darting away. A single Geist dies easily; a swarm does not.
L	Grunt	Unggoy. The Covenant's laborers and cannon fodder: short, methane-breathing, and brave only in numbers. A Grunt fights while there is an officer to fear; kill its Elite and the squad is liable to scatter, shrieking. Left alone with a plasma grenade and nothing to lose, it may run at you holding one in each hand.
L	GruntHeavy	A Grunt trusted with a fuel rod cannon and armor to match. Heavies hang back and lob green bolts that arc over cover; close the distance quickly or keep moving.
L	GruntSpecOps	Unggoy special operations: black armor, a better weapon and the discipline the rank and file lack. They follow the Spec Ops Elites onto the hard objectives and are far slower to break.
L	GruntUltra	An Unggoy veteran in white armor, survivor of more campaigns than its kin can count. Ultras stand their ground longer, take more punishment and lead lesser Grunts when no Elite is near.
L	Hunter	Mgalekgolo. Not one creature but a colony of orange worms living as one armored giant, always deployed as a bonded pair. Their front is almost impervious; aim for the exposed orange flesh at the neck and back, and do not stand still when one lowers its shield to charge. Kill one and its brother will go berserk.
L	HunterMajor	A veteran Mgalekgolo in red armor, its arm cannon replaced by a flamethrower. It is harder to kill than the common Hunter, and it wants to get close. Do not let it.
L	HunterUltra	The most seasoned of the Mgalekgolo, armored in white and the toughest of its kind. Its arm cannon is a plasma caster, lobbing bolts over walls and into cover.
L	Jackal	Kig-Yar. Raiders and mercenaries with the keenest eyes in the Covenant, fighting behind a wrist-mounted energy shield. The shield is overcharged plasma's natural prey; otherwise, wait for the gap when it fires and shoot past the edge.
L	JackalMajor	A Kig-Yar of standing, its shield colored by rank. Majors are steadier under fire and carry better arms than the pistol-toting Minors.
L	StealthElite	An Elite wearing an active camouflage harness. Watch for the shimmer as it moves, and for the moment it becomes visible to fire.
